.rem The cell writer's default vocabulary: one alias per pica
.rem construct, each painting one row's text in that construct's
.rem ink. The writer wraps and places every line; an alias only
.rem inks. An app replaces this file whole by supplying its own
.rem definitions of the same names to Render.
.rem
.rem Whole-line aliases receive a line that starts at the cursor.
.rem The writer places the title centered on row 0 of the first
.rem screen; the alias paints the bar and the text and never
.rem positions. The pen is restored after every use, so no alias
.rem resets it.
.def title
.fg white
.bg blue
.fill
$title
.enddef
.def byline
$byline
.enddef
.def heading
.fg yellow
$heading
.enddef
.def subheading
.fg cyan
$subheading
.enddef
.def tablehead
.fg cyan
$tablehead
.enddef
.def total
.fg yellow
$total
.enddef
.def rights
$rights
.enddef
.rem Span aliases overpaint part of a row the writer has already
.rem painted in default ink.
.def label
.fg cyan
$label
.enddef
.def emph
.fg white
$emph
.enddef
.rem t paints a line as written, whatever it begins with: the
.rem writer's every plain line goes through it.
.def t
$t
.enddef
